    {"id":"o-note","type":"text","x":1740,"y":1712,"width":300,"height":44,"strokeColor":"#9aa1ab","roughness":0,"groupIds":["O","lane2"],"text":"iOS only - Play does no local verification, so a bad\ntoken is refused by the service instead. cancelled:\nnothing. other errors: today's Purchase error alert.","fontSize":8.5,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"center","autoResize":false,"index":"a15j","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.7254901960784312},
    {"id":"o-capt","type":"text","x":1740,"y":1790,"width":300,"height":14,"strokeColor":"#5b21b6","roughness":0,"groupIds":["O","lane2"],"text":"B5.  What the sheet returns","fontSize":11,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a15k","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.2727272727272727},
    {"id":"o-capb","type":"text","x":1740,"y":1810,"width":340,"height":66,"strokeColor":"#6b7280","roughness":0,"groupIds":["O","lane2"],"text":"Two of these are states on BadgeState, not alerts: Paid, which\nthe worker retries, and Waiting, which holds nothing but the\nslot - Support SimpleX must not offer a second purchase of a\nconsumable. Both resolve through the store, not the service:\nTransaction.updates on iOS, queryPurchasesAsync on Play,\nwhich is also how each is re-found after a restart.","fontSize":9,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a15l","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.2222222222222223},
