    {"id":"d1-btnt","type":"text","x":100,"y":2522,"width":220,"height":14,"strokeColor":"#ffffff","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D1","lane3"],"text":"Redeem","fontSize":11,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"d1-btn","index":"a21a","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.2727272727272727},
    {"id":"d1-note","type":"text","x":80,"y":2566,"width":260,"height":24,"strokeColor":"#9aa1ab","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D1","lane3"],"text":"opened by Buy in browser at the same\nmoment as the browser, and waiting","fontSize":9,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"center","autoResize":false,"index":"a21b","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.3333333333333333},
    {"id":"d1-capt","type":"text","x":60,"y":2680,"width":300,"height":14,"strokeColor":"#1c1e26","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D1","lane3"],"text":"D1.  Both halves at once","fontSize":11,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a21c","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.2727272727272727},
    {"id":"d1-capb","type":"text","x":60,"y":2700,"width":340,"height":66,"strokeColor":"#6b7280","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D1","lane3"],"text":"On desktop, Buy in browser opens the page and this screen\ntogether, so the code has somewhere to go the moment it\nappears. No new screen, no deep link, no A6 - the shipped\nflow, with one extra window. It is also the honest fallback for\nany platform where the scheme turns out not to work.","fontSize":9,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a21d","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.4666666666666666},
    {"id":"d2-panel","type":"rectangle","x":480,"y":2040,"width":300,"height":620,"strokeColor":"#8f97a3","backgroundColor":"#ffffff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"boundElements":[{"id":"ar-d1d2","type":"arrow"}],"index":"a220"},
    {"id":"d2-url","type":"rectangle","x":480,"y":2040,"width":300,"height":26,"strokeColor":"transparent","backgroundColor":"#eceef1","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"index":"a221"},
    {"id":"d2-urlt","type":"text","x":496,"y":2048,"width":268,"height":12,"strokeColor":"#9aa1ab","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"badges.simplex.chat/#/tier?app=desktop","fontSize":9,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a222","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.3333333333333333},
    {"id":"d2-title","type":"text","x":496,"y":2090,"width":268,"height":22,"strokeColor":"#1c1e26","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"Paid. Here is your code.","fontSize":16,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a223","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.375},
    {"id":"d2-code","type":"rectangle","x":496,"y":2128,"width":268,"height":36,"strokeColor":"#d6dae0","backgroundColor":"#f7f8fa","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"index":"a224"},
    {"id":"d2-codet","type":"text","x":500,"y":2140,"width":260,"height":14,"strokeColor":"#1c1e26","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"SB-4K2M9-XQ7VT-H3BNP-R8WLC","fontSize":10,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"center","autoResize":false,"index":"a225","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.4},
    {"id":"d2-btn","type":"rectangle","x":496,"y":2180,"width":268,"height":34,"strokeColor":"#0053d0","backgroundColor":"#ffffff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"boundElements":[{"id":"d2-btnt","type":"text"}],"index":"a226"},
    {"id":"d2-btnt","type":"text","x":506,"y":2190,"width":248,"height":14,"strokeColor":"#0053d0","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"Copy code","fontSize":11,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"d2-btn","index":"a227","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.2727272727272727},
    {"id":"d2-qr","type":"rectangle","x":496,"y":2236,"width":110,"height":110,"strokeColor":"#d6dae0","backgroundColor":"#f7f8fa","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"index":"a228"},
    {"id":"d2-qrt","type":"text","x":496,"y":2352,"width":110,"height":24,"strokeColor":"#9aa1ab","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"scan to carry it\nto your phone","fontSize":9,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"center","autoResize":false,"index":"a229","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.3333333333333333},
    {"id":"d2-redeem","type":"text","x":622,"y":2236,"width":142,"height":36,"strokeColor":"#1c1e26","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"REDEEM IT IN THE APP\nThe Redeem code screen\nis already open.","fontSize":8.5,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a22a","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.411764705882353},
    {"id":"d2-warn","type":"rectangle","x":622,"y":2288,"width":142,"height":58,"strokeColor":"transparent","backgroundColor":"#fdf3e7","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"index":"a22b"},
    {"id":"d2-warnt","type":"text","x":632,"y":2298,"width":122,"height":38,"strokeColor":"#8a5a1e","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"This is the only copy.\nSaved in this browser\nand nowhere else.","fontSize":8.5,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a22c","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.4901960784313726},
    {"id":"d2-capt","type":"text","x":480,"y":2680,"width":300,"height":14,"strokeColor":"#1c1e26","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"D2.  The page, told which app it is","fontSize":11,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a22d","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.2727272727272727},
    {"id":"d2-capb","type":"text","x":480,"y":2700,"width":340,"height":66,"strokeColor":"#6b7280","roughness":0,"groupIds":["D2","lane3"],"text":"codeIssued as it ships, with one line changed. The app builds\nthe URL, so ?app=desktop is a fact rather than a guess -\nbetter than sniffing the user agent, which cannot tell a\ndesktop browser opened by SimpleX from any other. Mobile\ngets ?app=true and the A5 screen instead.","fontSize":9,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a22e","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.4666666666666666},
    {"id":"q-box","type":"rectangle","x":900,"y":2040,"width":1540,"height":260,"strokeColor":"#e0a672","backgroundColor":"#ffffff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["Q","lane3"],"index":"a230"},
    {"id":"q-head","type":"text","x":924,"y":2064,"width":900,"height":20,"strokeColor":"#a15c1e","roughness":0,"groupIds":["Q","lane3"],"text":"QUESTIONS - deep links, and whether the desktop can have them at all","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a231","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.3333333333333333},
    {"id":"q-body","type":"text","x":924,"y":2098,"width":1490,"height":130,"strokeColor":"#4b5563","roughness":0,"groupIds":["Q","lane3"],"text":"1.  Desktop has no scheme handler today. Nothing in the desktop module registers one and nothing handles it: appOpenUrl is wired in commonMain but has no desktop plumbing, and\n     desktop/build.gradle.kts declares only Deb, Dmg, Msi and Exe with no protocol entry. Adding one is per-OS work - CFBundleURLTypes plus setOpenURIHandler on macOS, registry keys\n     the MSI would have to write on Windows, a .desktop file with x-scheme-handler/simplexchat on Linux - and it would still not cover an unpackaged run. Hence D1: desktop does not wait for it.\n\n2.  Will a browser follow it without a tap? The attempt is made from a hidden frame, so a refusal stays inside the frame rather than replacing the screen with an error page that would\n     put the code into history. Expect nothing to happen on iOS Safari, which has ignored custom schemes in frames for years, nor on Chrome, which blocks a gestureless external-protocol\n     launch - and a payment settling minutes after the last tap has no gesture. So Return to SimpleX is the real path. What is left is to try it on devices once the app registers the scheme.","fontSize":10,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a232","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.4444444444444444},
    {"id":"n-box","type":"rectangle","x":900,"y":2340,"width":1540,"height":300,"strokeColor":"#c9ced6","backgroundColor":"#ffffff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"roughness":0,"roundness":{"type":3},"groupIds":["N","lane3"],"index":"a233"},
    {"id":"n-head","type":"text","x":924,"y":2364,"width":900,"height":20,"strokeColor":"#1c1e26","roughness":0,"groupIds":["N","lane3"],"text":"What has to be built, and what it costs","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a234","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.3333333333333333},
    {"id":"n-body","type":"text","x":924,"y":2398,"width":1490,"height":220,"strokeColor":"#4b5563","roughness":0,"groupIds":["N","lane3"],"text":"The browser lane needs nothing from the service: the code purchase runs exactly as it ships, the browser mints the code and sends only its SHA-256, and the only reason the buyer\nnever sees one is that the link carries it instead of the screen. The store lane is the part that does need service work - purchaseBadge has to accept a store receipt and verify it,\nand no provider adapter for that exists today.\n\nThe page needs three things: read the app flag from the fragment and start at Choose your badge; at the end, try the deep link and offer Return to SimpleX with Show code under it;\nand for ?app=desktop, keep showing codeIssued as it does now.\n\nThe app needs: Buy in browser without its confirm alert; a handler for the new link; A6, a spinner around the existing apiRedeemBadgeCode; on desktop, opening Redeem code alongside\nthe browser; and for the store lane, B4's checkout and the two BadgeState outcomes behind B5.\n\nWhat it costs: the app cannot show a price before sending the buyer out, because it has no catalog - Buy in browser is a leap into a page. And the code still exists, so it can be\nintercepted, screenshotted from the backup button, or pasted somewhere else. Hidden is not the same as absent.","fontSize":10,"fontFamily":2,"autoResize":false,"index":"a235","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":2},
    {"id":"ar-d1d2","type":"arrow","x":368,"y":2350,"width":104,"height":0,"strokeColor":"#a15c1e","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":0,"elbowed":true,"points":[[0,0],[104,0]],"startArrowhead":"arrow","endArrowhead":"arrow","boundElements":[{"id":"ar-d1d2-t","type":"text"}],"index":"a250","fillStyle":"solid"},
    {"id":"ar-d1d2-t","type":"text","x":370.23193359375,"y":2337,"width":99.5361328125,"height":26,"strokeColor":"#a15c1e","roughness":0,"text":"opened together, code\ncarried by hand","fontSize":10,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"ar-d1d2","index":"a251","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"originalText":"opened together, code carried by hand","lineHeight":1.3},
    {"id":"ft-note","type":"text","x":60,"y":2830,"width":2400,"height":26,"strokeColor":"#6b7280","roughness":0,"groupIds":["footer"],"text":"Copy is quoted from the app and the page. The app's screens take the page's names: Your level becomes Choose your badge, the level name becomes How long?, and Check your order is shared already.\nStore prices are illustrative and come from the storefront; the page's prices are the shipped catalog. Not drawn: the page's refusals - no active price, a provider unavailable, too many attempts - which are unchanged and already built.","fontSize":10,"fontFamily":2,"index":"a300","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"lineHeight":1.3}
  ],
  "appState": {"gridSize": 20, "gridStep": 5, "gridModeEnabled": false, "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff"},
  "files": {}
}
